{"id":"translate-body-en-cenc-m71","capability":"translate_body_en","what":"同一条地震稿的中文正文，逐块译成英文（整块译完，不是只译首句）","match":{"includes":["中国地震台网中心正式测定"]},"reply":{"blockMap":[{"includes":["中国地震台网中心正式测定"],"en":"<p>The China Earthquake Networks Center formally measured a magnitude 7.1 earthquake at 06:12 Beijing time on 21 November 2026 near the Yarlung Tsangpo suture in southern Tibet, at a focal depth of 12 km, about 38 km from the nearest county seat, with a maximum intensity of VIII. In its bulletin the center listed the main-shock parameters, the aftershock sequence and station arrivals. The USGS put the same event at Mw 7.0, with an epicenter on the Yarlung Tsangpo suture about 9 km from the Chinese fix. The difference in magnitude and location is a normal difference of measurement basis, and readers should keep both figures. By 12:00 on 21 November the area had recorded one M 5.2 aftershock about 41 km from the main shock. The Tibet transport department inspected the G318 corridor and found no blocked section; the emergency management department sent a working group to townships near the epicenter to check buildings and people.</p>"}]},"author":"英文编辑（GEOHOT 英文腿，2026-11-23 核过中文稿与原文）"}
